activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8759911Z **Creating a Pull Request**
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8760223Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8760431Z To create a pull request:
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8761093Z 1. Make any file changes directly in the working directory.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8762225Z 2. If you haven't done so already, create a new local branch using `git checkout -b <branch-name>` with an appropriate unique name.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8764146Z 3. Add and commit your changes to the branch. Be careful to add exactly the files you intend, and check there are no extra files left un-added. Verify you haven't deleted or changed any files you didn't intend to.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8765949Z 4. Do not push your changes. That will be done by the tool.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8767137Z 5. Create the pull request with the create_pull_request tool from safeoutputs exactly once, only when the final title/body/branch are ready.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8769713Z 6. After calling `create_pull_request`, STOP. Do not probe with another PR call, do not test auth with manual `git push`, and do not rewrite git remotes.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8770726Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8774477Z **Important**: The `branch` parameter in the create_pull_request tool **must exactly match the name of your current local git branch** — the branch you just committed to. You can verify this with `git branch --show-current`. Never invent or guess a branch name; always use the actual branch name from `git branch --show-current`. If you are on an existing branch (e.g. you checked out a PR branch), use that branch name.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8777147Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8779327Z **Important**: `create_pull_request` is not a sandbox. Every successful call records a real PR intent that can become an externally visible pull request. Never use placeholder payloads like `"test"` / `"test"` to see what happens. If you are not ready to open the real PR, use `noop` or `report_incomplete` instead.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8781539Z </safe-output-tools>
