activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8792514Z ```
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8792725Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8793339Z To inject an entire local file as the `body` field without re-embedding its content in the model context, use `jq -Rs`:
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8794291Z ```bash
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8794759Z jq -Rs --arg discussion_number "$DISCUSSION_NUMBER" \
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8795491Z   '{discussion_number: ($discussion_number|tonumber), body: .}' \
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8796175Z   discussion-body.md \
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8796671Z   | safeoutputs update_discussion .
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8797168Z ```
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8798621Z `jq -Rs` reads the file as a raw string (`-R`) and slurps it into a single JSON string value (`-s`), so `body` is always a valid JSON field. Piping `cat file | safeoutputs ...` does not populate `body` and will be rejected.
