activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8835469Z # Modernization Implement
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8835769Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8835982Z Implement the Rust port of `TIMCNV`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8836326Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8836529Z ## What you may and may not write
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8836848Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8837215Z You may write **only** files under `modern/src/`. That is enforced by the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8838137Z safe-output configuration, not by your good behaviour, and it is deliberate:
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8839308Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8839683Z - `legacy/src/**` is the **oracle**. It defines correct. If you could edit it,
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8840488Z   "the port matches the legacy deck" would mean nothing.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8841315Z - `legacy/tests/golden/**` and `legacy/tests/expected/**` are the **evidence**.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8842254Z   Byte-for-byte equivalence against a file you were allowed to rewrite is not
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8842996Z   evidence of anything.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8843603Z - `modern/tests/**` is the **judge**. You do not get to grade your own
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8844441Z   homework. If a test fails, the test is right and you are wrong.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8844921Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8845304Z If you believe a test is genuinely incorrect, do not work around it. Say so in
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8846457Z the pull request body and let a human decide.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8846873Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8847096Z ## The constraint that shapes everything
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8847460Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8847850Z This is flight-qualified ground software for a satellite in operation. The
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8849128Z output of `legacy/src/geosat.f` is parsed by a downstream archive loader by
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8850072Z fixed column position. The bar is not "works" or "looks idiomatic". The bar is
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8850919Z **byte-for-byte identical output on every golden vector**.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8851367Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8851830Z That includes reproducing behaviour that looks wrong. If the legacy routine has
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8852785Z a defect, port the defect. Record it in the pull request body under a heading
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8853712Z `Preserved defects` so a human can schedule fixing it as its own change with
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8854626Z its own updated vectors. Fixing a defect while porting it destroys the only
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8855377Z proof you have that the port is faithful.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8855910Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8856115Z ## Before you write anything
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8858863Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8859341Z 1. Read `docs/plans/<routine-lowercase>.md` if it exists. That plan was
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8860598Z    reviewed by a human. Follow it. If you are going to deviate, say why in the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8861353Z    pull request body.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8862031Z 2. Read the routine in `legacy/src/geosat.f`. Read the COMMON blocks it touches
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8863139Z    in `legacy/src/geosat.inc`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8863970Z 3. Read `legacy/graphify-out/graph.json` to see what calls the routine and what
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8864785Z    it calls, so you know the blast radius.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8865553Z 4. Read `modern/src/precision.rs`. It defines the numeric contract for this
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8866935Z    port -- when to use `f32`, how transcendentals are evaluated, why expression
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8869387Z    order matters. Every arithmetic decision you make must follow it.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8870469Z 5. Read a neighbouring module that is already ported -- `modern/src/crc.rs` is
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8872395Z    short and representative -- to match the house style.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8873199Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8873442Z ## Numeric rules, non-negotiable
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8873774Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8874178Z The legacy deck declares everything `REAL(4)`. Getting this wrong produces
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8875138Z output that is correct to three decimal places and still fails.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8875621Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8876641Z - Every intermediate value is `f32`. Do not compute in `f64` and round at the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8877942Z   end -- that double-rounds and diverges.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8879263Z - Preserve **expression order exactly** as written in the FORTRAN. `a * b * c`
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8880262Z   rounds after each operation. Reassociating changes the result.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8887752Z - Transcendentals go through `modern/src/precision.rs`, never `f32::sin` and
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8889598Z   friends directly.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8891253Z - Integer-to-float conversion is `as f32`, matching FORTRAN `REAL(INT)`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8891868Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8892055Z ## Proving it
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8892298Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8892642Z Run these. All of them. Do not open a pull request until they pass.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8893158Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8893340Z ```
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8893731Z cd modern && cargo test
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8894797Z ```
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8895359Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8895789Z That runs the characterization suite, which pipes all four golden vectors
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8896734Z through both the compiled 1987 binary and your Rust port and compares the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8897524Z output byte for byte. It also runs the unit suite.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8898054Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8899112Z If `cargo test` fails, you are not done. Read the diff, fix the port, run it
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8900536Z again. Do not weaken a test -- you cannot, the fencing forbids it, and
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8901532Z attempting it will fail the run.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8901895Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8902146Z ## The pull request body
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8902757Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8903114Z Write it for a reviewer who will not read your diff line by line:
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8904289Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8904811Z 1. **What the routine does** -- in plain language, cited to `geosat.f:LINE`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8978765Z 2. **How the port proves it** -- name the vectors, state that `cargo test`
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8979651Z    passes, give the count.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8980356Z 3. **Preserved defects** -- anything you reproduced on purpose that looks
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8981146Z    wrong, and what fixing it later would require.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8981906Z 4. **Numeric decisions** -- any place expression order or precision was
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8982741Z    load-bearing, so the reviewer knows where to look hardest.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8983578Z 5. **What you did not do** -- gaps, assumptions, anything you were unsure of.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8984475Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8984658Z ## Rules
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8984879Z 
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8985282Z - Write only under `modern/src/`. The safe-output configuration enforces this.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8986243Z - Never edit the legacy deck, the golden vectors, the expected output, or the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8986970Z   tests.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.8988152Z - A draft pull request is the only output. Approving a port is a human's call.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.9051708Z - If the routine is already fully implemented and `cargo test` passes with no
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.9052818Z   changes from you, do not invent work. Call `report_incomplete` and say the
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.9053596Z   routine is already ported.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.9054241Z - If the named routine does not exist in the deck, say so and call
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.9054963Z   `report_incomplete`.
activation	Print prompt	2026-08-24T16:43:59.9055256Z 
